 <kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-5239066-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>5239066</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-5239067-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>5239067</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-5255855-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>5255855</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-59139339-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>59139339</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1044953A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>DAICEL CHEM</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKADA MASAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DAICEL CHEMICAL INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, MASAYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKADA MASAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, MASAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for the preparation of alkaline earth metal salts of  beta -diketo compounds by using one mole of a powdery or granular alkaline earth metal compound and at least 2.04 moles of an aliphatic  beta -diketo compound. The reaction may be conducted either by feeding both components into a reactor continuously or intermittently or by adding either of the components to the other continuously or intermittently. The maximum reaction temperature may reach 50  DEG C or above, and the reaction mixture may be aged, followed by drying in an inert gas atmosphere at 100 to 180  DEG C. The alkaline earth metal compound may be calcium hydroxide, magnesium hydroxide or barium hydroxide, while the aliphatic  beta -diketo compound may be a compound represented by general formula (1), particularly, acetoacetic ester or acetylacetone. The process can give high-quality and stable alkaline earth metal salts of  beta -diketo compounds.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un procédé de préparation de sels de composés  beta -dicéto de métaux alcalino-terreux à partir d'une mole d'un composé pulvérulent ou granulaire d'un métal alcalino-terreux et d'au moins 2,04 moles d'un composé aliphatique  beta -dicéto. La réaction peut se conduire soit en alimentant un réacteur au moyen des deux composés en continu ou par intermittence, soit en ajoutant l'un des composés à l'autre en continu ou par intermittence. La température maximale de réaction peut atteindre 50 DEG  ou plus, et le mélange réactif peut être vieilli, puis séché dans une atmosphère de gaz inerte entre 100  DEG C et 180  DEG C. Le composé de métal alcalino-terreux peut être un hydroxyde de calcium, de magnésium ou de baryum, tandis que le composé aliphatique  beta -dicéto peut être un composé de formule générale (1), et en particulier un ester acétoacétique ou de l'acétylacétone. Les sels ainsi obtenus sont stables et de qualité élevée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>